From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:50:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 79/83] flashnext_mia: the four settings upstream's Flash Next
 also reads keep its one row each

Upstream main registered TF_FLASHNEXT_CONFIDENCE, _KEEP_LATE, _PROFILE and _SHARED_SIDE in its
flashnext scope. Her rows for the same names came first in the table, so upstream's engine
read them by her forms (SHARED_SIDE took on and off), and two environment tests failed.
Her rows for the four are gone; her engine checks their flashnext rows when it opens
(cuda_env.shared), and a test holds every setting to one row. SHARED_SIDE now takes 0 or 1.
